# Global Systems First (ABSOLUTE — ALWAYS ON)

**Highest-priority engineering rule for this repo.** Applies to **every** file change, fix proposal, and refactor — not only skills, not only when the user repeats it.

The project owner must **not** have to re-explain this. Agents enforce it on **every turn** without being asked.

## Priority order (when rules conflict)

1. **This rule** + `.cursor/rules/no-bandaid-fixes.mdc` + `.cursor/rules/skill-global-rules.mdc` + `.cursor/rules/move-preview-intent-truth.mdc`
2. Roadmap / phase gates / architecture skills (`Simulator`, layers, timeline, `AbilitySystem`)
3. Convenience, speed, “small local fix,” model-default shortcuts

If a proposed edit violates (1) to satisfy (3) → **do not implement** until redesigned or the owner approves a documented exception.

## Every edit must

1. **Use the existing global system** that owns the behavior (sim, director, `AbilitySystem`, commit slots, data definitions, overlay derived from slots — not parallel logic).
2. **Minimize heuristics** — no second state machines, no UI-only flags that commit path ignores, no cursor/preview/click paths that disagree.
3. **Extend the canonical path** — one truth pipeline; preview == execution where applicable.
4. **Prefer data** over `if ability.id == …` / per-unit branches.
5. **Remove** the obsolete path in the same change when replacing behavior.

## Heuristic (forbidden unless owner-approved exception)

A **heuristic** here means: behavior driven by a local shortcut that is **not** the same rule the rest of the feature uses — e.g. a flag only presentation reads, a special case only one skill uses, a fix that makes hover/click disagree with `commit_from_slots`.

**Default: zero new heuristics.** Fix the owner system instead.

### Examples that **are** heuristics (must be named — never report as `none`)

| Pattern | Example (this repo) |
|---------|---------------------|
| Tab- or screen-only apply | UI scale preview only on Interface tab; Display tab unchanged |
| Node/widget identity at apply time | `if lbl == _ui_scale_label` instead of shared applier / data tier |
| Parallel apply paths | `save_to_disk` + `changed` but combat never reloads; separate preview function |
| Presentation-only state | Slider moves a local var UI reads; `GameSettings` / commit path unchanged |
| Per-id / per-scene branch | `if ability.id == …` when `.tres` / `EffectData` could express it |

### Examples that are **not** heuristics (still name the canonical owner)

| Pattern | Example (this repo) |
|---------|---------------------|
| Single shared applier | `GameSettings` → `MenuInterfaceApplier.apply(root, settings)` on whole tree |
| Data/meta at **build**, type rules at **apply** | `menu_font_tier` meta + walk by `Control` type — not `if node == _foo` |
| One reload+apply bus | `EventBus.interface_settings_changed` → owner `_on_display_settings_applied` |

## Heuristics audit (mandatory — before declaring `none`)

**Forbidden:** Writing `Heuristics added: none` as a default footer, ritual checkbox, or without completing the audit below. **Claiming `none` without walking the table is a rule violation** — same severity as inventing a heuristic silently.

**Process (every plan, edit, or fix turn with code changes):**

1. Name **Global system used** (canonical owner file/API).
2. Walk **every row** of the audit table below.
3. If **any row fails** → list each failure under **Heuristics added** (short name + one line), or **redesign** before merge.
4. If **all rows pass** → you may write `none`, but you **must** include a one-line **Heuristics audit** summary proving you walked the table (not just the word `none`).

Owner may ask **“Walk the table”** — you must answer each row in plain language. Inability to do so means the `none` claim was invalid.

| # | Audit question | Pass requires |
|---|----------------|---------------|
| 1 | **Single owner** | The listed global system owns this behavior end-to-end — no parallel owner |
| 2 | **One apply path** | No second preview / save / commit / combat path that can diverge |
| 3 | **No identity branches** | No `if node == …`, `if tab == …`, `if scene == …` for this behavior (unless owner approved ⚠ exception) |
| 4 | **No UI-only state** | No flag/meta only presentation reads that sim/commit/`GameSettings` ignore |
| 5 | **Reusable** | Another screen/feature could use the same path without a new special-case branch |
| 6 | **Obsolete path removed** | Replacing a hack deletes the old path in the **same** change |

## Mandatory: exception warning (no silent bypass)

If the **correct** fix requires **breaking, bypassing, or adding an exception to** a global system, you **must stop** and post this block **before any edit**:

```
## ⚠ Global system exception (approval required)

**Global rule / system affected:** (name the system + file/API, e.g. commit slots, AbilitySystem.can_use, timeline column rule)

**Why the global path is insufficient:** (one paragraph — root cause, not symptom)

**Proposed exception:** (exact behavior change — what would diverge from the global rule)

**Alternatives considered:** (at least one way to stay on the global system, even if harder)

**Is this acceptable?** (yes / no / suggest alternative)
```

- Do **not** implement the exception until the owner replies **yes** to that specific exception.
- Do **not** hide exceptions in changelog prose — use the block above.
- “User said fix it fast” is **not** approval.

## Mandatory disclosure (every agent turn — no exceptions)

Any response that **proposes, implements, or summarizes** a code or rule change MUST include **both** lines below, visibly (not buried in prose):

- **Global system used:** (canonical owner — file/API; e.g. `_build_commit_slots_at_cell` → `commit_from_slots`)
- **Heuristics audit:** one line — either `rows 1–6 pass: …` (how you know) **or** `row N fail: …`
- **Heuristics added:** `none` OR each heuristic named (only after audit; see **Heuristics audit** above)

**`Heuristics added: none` without `Heuristics audit:` = invalid** — treat as if heuristics were undisclosed.

**Required in:**
- Permission gate / plans (`interpret-plan-permission.mdc`)
- Post-implementation summaries and fix explanations (including bug-fix replies)
- **## Changelog** on every edit turn (`living-sandbox-architect.mdc`, `AGENTS.md`) — dedicated `### Global systems` subsection

**Omit only** on pure read-only Q&A with **no** proposed or completed changes.

**Omitting any of the three lines = rule violation** — same severity as skipping the permission gate or auto-commit.

## Canonical global systems (Honor & Iron — non-exhaustive)

| Domain | Global owner |
|--------|----------------|
| Planning commit / cursor / preview | **Move preview is intent truth** (`.cursor/rules/move-preview-intent-truth.mdc`) — same slots path: `_build_commit_slots_at_cell` → `_finalize_commit_slots` → `CombatDirector.commit_from_slots` / `preview_commit_valid`; commit ratifies preview, never rewrites it |
| Ability legality / range / targeting | `AbilitySystem` + ability data |
| Turn resolution | `Simulator.simulate` — headless, no Nodes |
| Skills / economy | Timeline columns, AP/MP, `EffectData` — see `skill-global-rules.mdc` |
| Living sandbox / map VFX | `sandbox_map_system.md`, `EffectsSettings`, GPU shaders — see `living-sandbox-architect.mdc` |

When unsure which system owns a behavior → **read and extend that system**; do not add a presentation-only workaround.

